Part II — The Typed Uncertainty Structure

Chapter 3. The Four Uncertainties

3.1 Semantic uncertainty

Definition 3.1. Let \{\mathcal X^{(k)}\}_{k \in K} be a family of measurable state spaces, each carrying a scientific definition of X^{(k)}. The semantic uncertainty is the family

\mathcal U_{\mathrm{var}} = \{(\mathcal X^{(k)}, \sigma^{(k)})\}_{k \in K}

with \sigma^{(k)} the semantic specification of \mathcal X^{(k)}.

3.2 Observational uncertainty

Definition 3.2. For instrument class i, the observational uncertainty is a Markov kernel U_{\mathrm{obs}}^{(i)}: \mathcal X \rightsquigarrow \mathcal O_i sending state to a distribution on recorded values, conditional on the inference chain \ell_i.

3.3 Stochastic uncertainty

Definition 3.3. Let U denote exogenous forcing. The stochastic uncertainty is the Markov kernel

U_{\mathrm{stoch}}: \mathcal X \times \mathcal U \rightsquigarrow \mathcal X, \qquad (x, u) \mapsto P_\xi(\cdot \mid x, u).

3.4 Model uncertainty

Definition 3.4. Let \mathfrak F = \{F_\theta : \mathcal X \times \mathcal U \rightsquigarrow \mathcal X\}_{\theta \in \Theta_F} be a class of admissible dynamical models, with admissibility protocol A_F:

F_\theta \in \mathfrak F \iff A_F(F_\theta) = 1.

The model uncertainty is the pair (\mathfrak F, A_F).

3.5 The typed uncertainty structure

Definition 3.5. The typed uncertainty of an estimation is

\mathcal U(X) = (\mathcal U_{\mathrm{var}}, \mathcal U_{\mathrm{obs}}, \mathcal U_{\mathrm{stoch}}, \mathcal U_{\mathrm{model}}).

This is a tuple, not a vector. Its components live in different categories and are maintained separately. The PSC does not claim ontological irreducibility of these classes; the separation is an architectural decision justified by the impossibility result of §4.

