Part III — The State Record

Chapter 5. Formal Definition of \mathcal S

Definition 5.1. A state record is a tuple

\mathcal S = (I, D, X, U, G, M, A, R, C, P)

with components:

· Identity I: (\mathrm{record\_id}, v, \mathrm{spatial\_id}, \mathrm{temporal\_id}, \mathrm{valid\_from}, \mathrm{valid\_to}), with v = (\mathrm{variable\_id}, \mathrm{definition\_version}). The pair v is immutable.
· Domain D: (\mathrm{semantics}, \mathrm{unit}, \mathrm{scale}, \rho_{\mathrm{sp}}, \rho_{\mathrm{t}}, \mathrm{aggregation}, \mathrm{range}).
· Estimate X: (\mathrm{value}, \mathrm{type}, \mathrm{support}, \mathrm{estimator\_id}), with \mathrm{type} \in \{\mathrm{scalar}, \mathrm{vector}, \mathrm{field}, \mathrm{distribution}, \mathrm{credal}, \mathrm{interval}, \mathrm{categorical}, \mathrm{set}, \mathrm{undefined}\}.
· Typed uncertainty U: (U_{\mathrm{var}}, U_{\mathrm{obs}}, U_{\mathrm{stoch}}, U_{\mathrm{model}}, \Delta_{\mathrm{dep}}, \mathrm{dilation\_status}, \mathrm{closure\_id}).
· Coverage G: (C_{\mathrm{sp}}, C_{\mathrm{t}}, \ell, E, \mathcal D, M_{\mathrm{miss}}, \mathcal B).
· Model state M: (\mathrm{model\_set\_id}, A_F^{(k)}, \mathrm{calibration\_scope}, \mathrm{validation\_scope}, \mathrm{closure\_op}^{(k)}).
· Anomaly A: (\Delta X, \partial_t X, \partial_t^2 X, \mathrm{derivative\_semantics}, \mathrm{anomaly\_status}, \mathrm{method\_id}, \mathrm{baseline\_id}, \mathrm{persistence}, \mathrm{extent}).
· Regime R: (\mathrm{label}, \Theta_R^{(k)}, \mathrm{transition\_status}).
· Criticality C: (\mathrm{status}, \Theta_C^{(k)}, \mathrm{sensitivity}, \mathrm{scope}).
· Provenance P: (\mathrm{refs}, \mathrm{parents}, \mathrm{supersedes}, \mathrm{superseded\_by}, \mathrm{timestamps}).

5.2 Temporal semantics

The record supports two modes via \tau_{\mathrm{sem}} \in \{\mathrm{snapshot}, \mathrm{interval}\}. Differencing is permitted only when both records share the same \tau_{\mathrm{sem}}, or when the interval summary operator is idempotent.

5.3 Completeness levels

\mathrm{comp}(\mathcal S) \in \{\mathrm{raw}, \mathrm{calibrated}, \mathrm{estimated}, \mathrm{classified}, \mathrm{evaluated}\}.

