Chapter 6. The Type System

Definition 6.1. The type universe comprises \mathsf{Var}(v), \mathsf{Obs}(i), \mathsf{Model}(\mathfrak F^{(k)}), \mathsf{Ref}_{\mathrm{regime}}(k), \mathsf{Ref}_{\mathrm{crit}}(k), \mathsf{Unc}_{\mathrm{var}}, \mathsf{Unc}_{\mathrm{obs}}, \mathsf{Unc}_{\mathrm{stoch}}, \mathsf{Unc}_{\mathrm{model}}, \mathsf{Cred}(\mathcal X), and \mathsf{Rec}.

Rule \Delta-compat.

\frac{\mathcal S_1: \mathsf{Rec}(v_1), \ \mathcal S_2: \mathsf{Rec}(v_2), \ \mathsf{Compatible}(v_1, v_2)}{\Delta(\mathcal S_1, \mathcal S_2) : \mathsf{Rec}(v_{12})}

Rule \Gamma_{\mathrm{agg}}-registered.

\frac{\mathcal U : \mathsf{Unc}^{\otimes 4}, \ \Gamma^{(k)} \in \mathrm{Reg}(\Gamma)}{\Gamma^{(k)}(\mathcal U): \mathsf{Scalar}}

Rule \Theta-required.

\frac{R \neq \bot \Rightarrow \Theta_R \neq \emptyset}{\vdash R : \mathsf{Regime}}

Rule \mathrm{closure}-registered.

\frac{\mathfrak F : \mathsf{Model}, \ \kappa^{(k)} \in \mathrm{Reg}(\mathrm{closure})}{\kappa^{(k)}(\mathfrak F) : \mathsf{Cred}(\mathcal X)}

Theorem 6.2 (Type soundness). Well-typed records enforce: (i) compatible definitions for \Delta X; (ii) registered aggregation for any scalar derived from \mathcal U; (iii) declared referentials for R and C; (iv) registered closure for any credal set derived from a model class.

