Chapter 7. Invariants

I1 (Semantic compatibility). \Delta X(v_1, v_2) defined only if \mathsf{Compatible}(v_1, v_2) = 1.

I2 (Uncertainty provenance). Every uncertainty object carries identifier, type, scope, method, and provenance. No bare scalar is valid.

I3 (Registered aggregation). A scalar V from \mathcal U exists only if \Gamma^{(k)} is registered.

I4 (Dependency). Operations requiring cross-component dependency are undefined when \Delta_{\mathrm{dep}} = \bot.

I5 (Coverage). Every estimate carries G \neq \emptyset.

I6 (Criticality). \Theta_C = \emptyset \Rightarrow C = \mathrm{undefined}.

I7 (Regime). \Theta_R = \emptyset \Rightarrow R = \mathrm{undefined}.

I8 (Revision). A new definition does not retroactively alter past records.

I9 (No-observation ⟹ no-claim). If no admissible observation constrains X_k on r, then X(r) may be typed \mathrm{undefined}.

I10 (Monotonicity under observation removal). Removing an observation cannot narrow the compatibility sets \mathcal C_\exists(Y) or \mathcal C_\forall(Y) on any variable. This invariant concerns constraint removal, not constraint addition.

I11 (Dilation recording). Let

\rho_k(\mathcal C) := \sup_{P, Q \in \mathcal C} W_2(\pi_k P, \pi_k Q)

be the marginal diameter of a credal set \mathcal C on coordinate k. If, upon adding an observation Y_{t+1}, there exists k with

\rho_k(\mathcal C_{t+1}(Y_{t+1})) > \rho_k(\mathcal C_t),

then the record must report \mathrm{dilation\_status} = \mathrm{present} with the affected coordinate k and the observation Y_{t+1}. Dilation is not suppressed.

I12 (Temporal causality in backtesting). Any evaluation at time t uses only observations from \{t' \leq t\}.

I13 (Registered closure). Any credal set derived from a model class \mathfrak F carries a reference to a registered closure operator \kappa^{(k)}. No closure is performed implicitly.

