Part V — Architecture

Chapter 10. The Federated Estimator

Definition 10.1. A PSC federation is a collection \{\mathcal E_\alpha\}_{\alpha \in A} of estimators on sub-domains \mathcal X_\alpha, with a fusion operator \Phi: \prod_\alpha \mathrm{Cred}(\mathcal X_\alpha) \to \mathrm{Cred}(\mathcal X) respecting \Delta_{\mathrm{dep}}.

Proposition 10.2. If \Delta_{\mathrm{dep}} = \bot, the fused set \mathcal C = \bigcap_\alpha \pi_\alpha^{-1}(\mathcal C_\alpha) is the largest consistent credal set.

Remark 10.3. Absence of dependency declaration does not imply independence; it implies maximal uninformative fusion under the constraint of marginal consistency.

Chapter 11. Registries

Definition 11.1. A PSC registry is R = (S_R, \mathrm{adm}_R, \mathrm{ver}_R, \mathrm{retire}_R) with schema, admission predicate, versioning policy, and retirement policy.

The PSC registries are:

· \mathrm{Reg}(\Gamma) — scalar aggregations;
· \mathrm{Reg}(\mathrm{closure}) — closure operators on model classes;
· \mathrm{Reg}(\sigma) — selections from credal sets;
· \mathrm{Reg}(A_F) — model admissibility protocols;
· \mathrm{Reg}(\Theta_R) — regime referentials;
· \mathrm{Reg}(\Theta_C) — criticality referentials;
· \mathrm{Reg}(\Delta_{\mathrm{dep}}) — dependency representations.

Proposition 11.2. A well-formed PSC record references only entries present in their registries at creation time. This is I3, I4, I6, I7, I13 in operational form.

