Appendix C. Registry Schemas

C.1 Aggregation Registry \mathrm{Reg}(\Gamma)

An entry of \mathrm{Reg}(\Gamma) is a tuple

(S_\Gamma, \mathrm{dom}_\Gamma, \mathrm{ass}_\Gamma, \mathrm{cal}_\Gamma, \mathrm{fals}_\Gamma, \mathrm{ver}_\Gamma)

with:

· S_\Gamma: schema of the aggregation operation (types of \mathcal U components consumed, type of scalar produced);
· \mathrm{dom}_\Gamma: declared domain of validity (spatial, temporal, variable scope);
· \mathrm{ass}_\Gamma: set of assumptions required;
· \mathrm{cal}_\Gamma: calibration procedure;
· \mathrm{fals}_\Gamma: falsification tests;
· \mathrm{ver}_\Gamma: versioning policy.

Rule. A scalar V derived from \mathcal U exists in a record iff the transformation \Gamma^{(k)} appears in \mathrm{Reg}(\Gamma) at the record's creation time (Invariant I3).

C.2 Closure Registry \mathrm{Reg}(\mathrm{closure})

An entry of \mathrm{Reg}(\mathrm{closure}) is a tuple

(S_\kappa, \mathrm{dom}_\kappa, \mathrm{props}_\kappa, \mathrm{ver}_\kappa)

with:

· S_\kappa: schema (input: model class \mathfrak F; output: credal set);
· \mathrm{dom}_\kappa: declared domain;
· \mathrm{props}_\kappa: declared mathematical properties (closed convex hull, \varepsilon-contamination, topological closure in a specified topology, etc.);
· \mathrm{ver}_\kappa: versioning policy.

Rule. Any credal set derived from a model class carries a reference to its closure operator (Invariant I13).

C.3 Selection Registry \mathrm{Reg}(\sigma)

An entry of \mathrm{Reg}(\sigma) is a tuple

(S_\sigma, \mathrm{dom}_\sigma, \mathrm{loss}_\sigma, \mathrm{equiv}_\sigma, \mathrm{fals}_\sigma, \mathrm{ver}_\sigma)

with:

· S_\sigma: schema (input: credal set; output: element of the credal set);
· \mathrm{dom}_\sigma: declared domain;
· \mathrm{loss}_\sigma: declared loss function or optimality criterion (Wasserstein barycenter, minimax, etc.);
· \mathrm{equiv}_\sigma: declared equivariance group, if any;
· \mathrm{fals}_\sigma: falsification tests;
· \mathrm{ver}_\sigma: versioning policy.

C.4 Dependency Registry \mathrm{Reg}(\Delta_{\mathrm{dep}})

An entry of \mathrm{Reg}(\Delta_{\mathrm{dep}}) is a tuple

(S_\Delta, \mathrm{type}_\Delta, \mathrm{dom}_\Delta, \mathrm{ass}_\Delta, \mathrm{ver}_\Delta)

with:

· S_\Delta: schema;
· \mathrm{type}_\Delta \in \{\mathrm{copula}, \mathrm{graphical}, \mathrm{vine}, \mathrm{OT}, \mathrm{moment}, \mathrm{other}\};
· \mathrm{dom}_\Delta: applicability conditions (dimension, marginal type);
· \mathrm{ass}_\Delta: assumptions;
· \mathrm{ver}_\Delta: versioning policy.

Rule. The type tag is mandatory. Copula entries are permitted only for d=2 with continuous marginals (Proposition 8.11, Corollary 8.13).

C.5 Referential Registries \mathrm{Reg}(\Theta_R), \mathrm{Reg}(\Theta_C)

Each entry is a tuple

(S_\Theta, \mathrm{criteria}_\Theta, \mathrm{scope}_\Theta, \mathrm{ver}_\Theta)

with declared thresholds, persistence requirements, irreversibility criteria, and scope.

Rule. A regime R or criticality C exists only with a declared referential (Invariants I6, I7).

